[coal] Adjust the code for vendor_cxx compatibility

Drake's vendor_cxx tool wraps each file's code in an inline namespace. It is
line-oriented, so it cannot see that a `namespace` block sits inside a
preprocessor conditional that Drake leaves undefined: it places the opening (or
closing) brace of the inline namespace inside the conditional, the preprocessor
then deletes that brace along with the rest of the block, and the inline
namespace is left unbalanced. In practice that swallows every header included
afterwards -- e.g., it lands <cmath> and <vector> inside `drake_vendor::std`.

Coal has three such blocks, all of which are dead code for Drake:

- fwd.hh ends with aliases for Coal's former name (hpp-fcl), guarded by
  COAL_BACKWARD_COMPATIBILITY_WITH_HPP_FCL. Drake does not use the hpp::fcl
  spelling and never defines that macro, so we delete the block. (The
  identical `#ifdef` in data_types.h needs no patch: that block is surrounded
  by ordinary code, so vendor_cxx wraps it correctly.)

- geometric_shapes.h forward-declares orgQhull::Qhull under COAL_HAS_QHULL,
  which Drake does not define because it does not build Coal's Qhull-based
  convex hull. A forward declaration is free, so rather than delete it we
  simply drop its guard.

- geometric_shapes.cpp opens with a COAL_HAS_QHULL block that mixes Qhull's
  #include statements with `using orgQhull::...` declarations. The
  declarations are the file's first line of code, so the inline namespace
  opens on them, inside the conditional. We move just the declarations to
  just after `namespace coal {`, where the conditional is bracketed by
  ordinary code. Every use of those names is inside namespace coal already,
  so this does not change what the Qhull build compiles.

Reasoning for not upstreaming this patch: Drake-specific vendoring.

--- include/coal/fwd.hh
+++ include/coal/fwd.hh
@@ -160,13 +160,4 @@
 typedef shared_ptr<const OcTree> OcTreeConstPtr_t;
 }  // namespace coal

-#ifdef COAL_BACKWARD_COMPATIBILITY_WITH_HPP_FCL
-namespace hpp {
-namespace fcl {
-using namespace coal;
-using Transform3f = Transform3s;  // For backward compatibility
-}  // namespace fcl
-}  // namespace hpp
-#endif
-
 #endif  // COAL_FWD_HH
--- include/coal/shape/geometric_shapes.h
+++ include/coal/shape/geometric_shapes.h
@@ -47,11 +47,9 @@
 #include "coal/data_types.h"
 #include "coal/shared_ptr_comparison.h"

-#ifdef COAL_HAS_QHULL
 namespace orgQhull {
 class Qhull;
 }
-#endif

 namespace coal {

--- src/shape/geometric_shapes.cpp
+++ src/shape/geometric_shapes.cpp
@@ -46,7 +46,11 @@
 #include <libqhullcpp/QhullVertexSet.h>
 #include <libqhullcpp/QhullRidge.h>
 #include <libqhullcpp/Qhull.h>
+#endif
+
+namespace coal {

+#ifdef COAL_HAS_QHULL
 using orgQhull::Qhull;
 using orgQhull::QhullFacet;
 using orgQhull::QhullPoint;
@@ -55,8 +59,6 @@
 using orgQhull::QhullVertexSet;
 #endif

-namespace coal {
-
 template <typename IndexType>
 ConvexBaseTpl<IndexType>* ConvexBaseTpl<IndexType>::convexHull(
     std::shared_ptr<std::vector<Vec3s>>& pts, unsigned int num_points,
